# NOTICE and credits

## What this repository is

Sovereign is a public case study of an air-gapped, on-premise AI deployment
for a law firm. It documents the infrastructure, states what it does not
contain, and writes down the alignment research questions that the
deployment's constraints raise.

## Provenance

This repository was derived from internal deployment artifacts of The Vault
AI, an on-premise legal AI project. The material was restructured for
publication: internal identifiers, credentials, matter content, and
operational details that would identify a firm or a person were removed.

The following artifacts are the basis for the technical content here:

* The cluster configuration and node-hardening procedures, which describe the
  enclave network topology, the hardware, the inference container
  specification, and the maintenance and failure-mode procedures.
* The document ingestion pipeline, which describes the poller, the parser
  with its OCR fallback threshold, the staged job directory, and the
  multi-pass extraction sequence.
* The case-centric data model, which describes the matter table, the
  per-matter panel table, the ledger table, the deadline table, the entity
  and processing tables, and the indexes and view over them.
* The container deployment kit, which describes the application and
  email-processor services, the persistent volumes, the health checks, and
  the configuration surface.

The field registry and grounding validator in `src/extraction_schema.py` were
written for this repository. They are an original implementation of ordinary
input validation and citation-grounding checks, not a port of any existing
code. The synthetic fixtures in `tests/fixtures/grounding_cases.json` were
written for this repository and describe no real matter.

## No client material

No client document, matter, caption, party name, or medical record content
appears anywhere in this repository. The source material was read to extract
architecture facts; matter content was deliberately not carried across.
`scripts/gate.py` enforces this, and the build fails if a matter-shaped
marker or a case-shaped filename appears.

## Third-party components referenced

The deployment described here uses open-weights models served by an
open-source inference runtime, and the references are to those projects by
name and configuration only. No third-party code is vendored into this
repository, and no model weights are redistributed.

The alignment framing in `README.md` is written in the register of publicly
published alignment research, including the "Recommendations for Technical AI
Safety Research Directions" post published by Anthropic's Alignment Science
team at <https://alignment.anthropic.com/2025/recommended-directions/>. That
post is cited as the framing reference for the open questions section. The
questions raised here are ours, and this repository is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or produced by that team.

